From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Do not run the stack sampling profiler in a Windows build

A build without Chrome branding counts as a local build, and those
profiled every browser, GPU and network process and a fifth of
renderers, each with a StackSamplingProfiler thread. Disable it on
Windows. A switch exists, but only the app could pass it (PLA-384).
Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-cef-trim.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 .../thread_profiler_platform_configuration.cc      |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/common/profiler/thread_profiler_platform_configuration.cc b/chrome/common/profiler/thread_profiler_platform_configuration.cc
index 98c125244f..278627f1c9 100644
--- a/chrome/common/profiler/thread_profiler_platform_configuration.cc
+++ b/chrome/common/profiler/thread_profiler_platform_configuration.cc
@@ -61,8 +61,14 @@ DefaultPlatformConfiguration::GetEnableRates(
   CHECK(IsSupportedForChannel(release_channel));
 
   if (!release_channel) {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
+    // Off on Windows: an embedder that must fit several processes in a small
+    // address space runs no sampling thread in each.
+    return RelativePopulations{100.0, 0.0, 0.0};
+#else
     // This is a local/CQ build.
     return RelativePopulations{0.0, 100.0, 0.0};
+#endif
   }
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
